We have long-term debt outstanding, excluding the current portion, with a fair market value of $15.3 billion and $9.2 billion as of December 31, 2024 and December 31, 2023, respectively. The fair value was less than the carrying value by $957 million at December 31, 2024, and $772 million less than the carrying value at December 31, 2023. A hypothetical 1% increase or decrease in interest rates would change the fair value by a decrease of 7% or an increase of 8%, respectively, at December 31, 2024.
We have selected hypothetical changes in foreign currency exchange rates, interest rates, and equity market prices to illustrate the possible impact of these changes; we are not predicting market events.
